  "description": "Change of use of the attached garage to a dog grooming studio and replacement of garage door with window.",
  "development_type": "Minor retail and service",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rPWE/G/1A, PWE/G/2, PWE/G/3, PWE/G/4, PWE/G/5, PWE/G/6, PWE/G/7, PWE/G/8, CIL form and Business Design & Access Statement\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The dog grooming use hereby approved shall only operate between the hours Monday to Friday 9am to 5pm and Saturday 10am to 5pm and all activity associated with the use shall cease outside of\rthese hours and days.\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r\r",
    "The use hereby permitted shall be restricted to a dog grooming business operated by a sole person, with no employees or other persons working from the premises at any time.  The use permitted shall occur only in the studio room as identified on drawing PWE/G/4.  The permitted use shall cease, and the room shall revert to residential use forming part of the dwelling at 19 Park Way if the dog grooming business ceases to operate from the premises. \r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r\r",
    "The number of customers on the premises shall not exceed one at any given time. All customer appointments in connection with the dog grooming use hereby permitted must be pre-arranged.  An appointment diary shall be maintained and be available for inspection on request by officers of the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r",
    "The dog grooming use hereby approved shall cater for the grooming of a maximum of 4 dogs per day, with only one dog on site to be groomed at any one time.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r",
    "Doors and windows shall be kept closed during dog grooming activities, except for access and egress.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of adjoining and nearby residential properties.\r",
    "There shall be no form of signage installed at the property in association with the proposed dog grooming use.\r\rReason: To retain the residential character and appearance of the streetscene.\r"
  ],
